{"commit":"7302e67","date":"2026-11-15T07:27:11-05:00","branch":"integrate","notes":[{"id":"screens-style-nov15","date":"2026-11-15","lines":["Every screen has a new look: smoky glass panels over the world, bigger lettering, and one bright amber button for the main thing to do.","A chosen game night, difficulty or character now shows a check mark, and the craft menu marks what you are missing with a cross.","The pause screen and the camp tent work with just a keyboard or just a controller: move with the arrows or d-pad, A or Enter picks, B resumes.","Going down shows a big banner saying how to get back up, and after a fall the title says what got you.","On the pause screen the river and the wind go quiet, and a computer joining someone else's game now shows what it is waiting for."]},{"id":"quality-pass-nov15","date":"2026-11-15","lines":["Inside houses, wolves and other creatures now walk on the floor instead of sinking into it up to their heads.","Bullets and arrows stop at floors and ceilings, and jumping under an upstairs floor no longer pokes your head into the room above.","House ceiling lamps hang above your head instead of in your face.","A torch goes out if you dive under water (T lights it again when you come up), and it no longer burns down while the game is paused.","The river's sound stops when a game ends."]},{"id":"worlds-fix-nov15","date":"2026-11-15","lines":["New random worlds are fixed: every one now has its Frostline cabin, and you can always climb out of the big lake at the end of the river."]},{"id":"start-menu-nov15","date":"2026-11-15","lines":["A new start menu in three steps: the title, then what you are playing (a ready-made game night, or your own mode and creatures), then who walks out. Back buttons and Esc go back a step.","How to play and Settings open from the title, and work with just a keyboard or just a controller."]},{"id":"torches-stumps-nov14","date":"2026-11-14","lines":["Carry a torch: craft a hand torch (wood and fiber) and it lights up the dark around you. It burns about a night, and any fire lights it again. T puts it away.","Hang torches on your walls and gate posts. At night wolves, hounds and rats keep back from a torch or a fire.","Dig up stumps (hold E by one) for a little wood and fiber. Leave a stump in the ground and a new tree grows back over a few days.","You can chop down the giant mushrooms now, for fiber and food. They grow back even faster."]},{"id":"running-water-nov14","date":"2026-11-14","lines":["Rivers run: ripples and white flecks drift downstream, faster where the river narrows, and you can hear the water as you get close.","Shores come alive: foam laps at the water's edge, wet stones and pebbles, driftwood and fallen trunks line the banks, and boulders stand out in the river."]},{"id":"houses-nov14","date":"2026-11-14","lines":["Ten kinds of houses on every new world: a two-storey farmhouse with a porch, a split-level, an L-shaped ranch, an A-frame cabin with a loft, a row of three joined houses, a shop with a flat upstairs, a stilt house in the Bog, an adobe house","Most have several rooms and floors to explore: climb the stairs, and in the A-frame the ladder to the loft","Rooms are furnished: beds, sofas, stoves, shelves of tins, a shop counter with its till","Porches now stand on posts and are built onto the house"]},{"id":"spider-poison-nov14","date":"2026-11-14","lines":["Spiders are tougher now: it takes more hits to bring one down.","A black widow's bite is poisonous: it keeps hurting for a few seconds, and the screen says Poisoned until it wears off.","A dying spider now curls up slowly instead of snapping shut."]},{"id":"places-nov14","date":"2026-11-14","lines":["New places to find on every new world: a radio tower you can climb, a crashed airliner, a frozen research station, a sunken barge, a giant mushroom ring, crater lakes and a hermit's island","Each place guards something worth having, and says its name when you first get there","Hold E at the radio tower's radio for 10 seconds to lift the fog and hear where every other place is","Bigger lakes have small islands to swim out to","The pause screen lists the places you have found or heard of, and which way they are"]},{"id":"switch-and-giveup-nov14","date":"2026-11-14","lines":["Change character at the camp: walk to the tent by the campfire and press E. You keep your pack, no need to leave and rejoin.","Animals no longer stand frozen over a fallen player: they give up the hunt and wander off."]},{"id":"spiders-nov14","date":"2026-11-14","lines":["Giant spiders now hunt in the Ruins and the Fungal Hollow. Their webs on the ground slow you down.","Spider nests keep sending spiders out until you tear them apart.","At night, watch the trees and ruined walls: a spider may come down on its thread right beside you.","Four kinds of spider, each its own size: the brown wolf spider, the pale spider of the Fungal Hollow, the black widow with the worst bite, and the huge shaggy brute."]},{"id":"repair-nov14","date":"2026-11-14","lines":["Fix your fort: hold H (d-pad right on a controller) by a damaged wall or gate to mend it, for a little wood (stone walls take metal). The Architect, the master builder, mends four times as fast for about half the wood.","A wall that falls leaves rubble for a little while: build the same wall back on it for half the price."]},{"id":"game-modes-nov14","date":"2026-11-14","lines":["Pick how to play together: Co-op or Free-for-all, with Easy, Normal or Hard creatures. The host chooses on the start menu or the pause screen.","Free-for-all: every weapon hurts everyone, rivals score points for creatures and knockouts, and a knocked-out player is back at their bed or the camp."]},{"id":"harder-and-fixes-nov14","date":"2026-11-14","lines":["More animals out there, in bigger packs, and they bite harder. Nightfall sends a pack after anyone outside the valley.","Players bump into each other instead of walking through.","Fires and torches light up much more around them.","Wood and other drops no longer get stuck inside rocks, and a joined player picks up what they touch.","Arrows fall out of an animal as soon as it dies.","Splashes when you wade through water or a tree falls into it. A felled birch leaves a white stump.","Build a gate on top of one of your walls to swap it in, for less than a new gate.","If the host's window is hidden, the world keeps going for everyone else.","Running down a steep hill no longer hurts like falling off a cliff.","The sleep screen tells you how to get up, and the game runs a little cooler on fast screens."]},{"id":"house-porches","date":"2026-11-12","lines":["Some houses in new worlds now have a little porch with a roof over the door. The first world, 20261103, is unchanged."]},{"id":"fog-of-war","date":"2026-11-12","lines":["Fog now closes in over ground you have never been near, and opens up where you have explored."]},{"id":"hunters-and-rocks","date":"2026-11-12","lines":["Creatures now come looking for you in every land and smell a wounded traveler from farther off, bog lurkers roam the Fungal Hollow, ledges are no longer safe from bears and wolves, rocks block you where they look, and the short freeze when "]},{"id":"creatures-pass","date":"2026-11-12","lines":["The bear is rebuilt from nose to tail: a shoulder hump, a dished face with proper eyes and nose, small round ears, big clawed paws and a thick grizzled coat. It walks like a bear, rears up to swipe, and rolls onto its side when it falls.","The ice crawler and the bog lurker are brand-new creatures, wolves and dust hounds have real coat markings, and the rat looks like a rat.","Every animal now flinches when you hit it and has its own way of falling, and wolves and hounds no longer skate on their paws when they stop."]},{"id":"background-music","date":"2026-11-12","lines":["Soft background music now plays, a gentler new take on the tune from the first Iron Wasteland. It turns darker at night, and quiets down whenever something happens. The Music slider in settings turns it down or off."]},{"id":"fireflies","date":"2026-11-12","lines":["Fireflies drift and blink over the meadows and the Bog after dusk."]},{"id":"health-number","date":"2026-11-10","lines":["Your health now shows as a number right on the health bar, like 85 / 100."]},{"id":"random-worlds","date":"2026-11-06","lines":["The mouse arrow stays hidden while you play, including after you close the craft menu","Every new game is a new world: its own hills, rivers, lakes and lands beyond the mountains. The safe valley and the camp are always at its heart.","Each world has a name on the start screen. Tell someone the name and they can play the same world, or press New world for another.","Joining a friend's game takes you to their world automatically."]},{"id":"play-logs","date":"2026-11-06","lines":["Every game you play is now saved and sent to Jared's Mac, so a problem can be found and fixed even if you did not notice it.","Press F9 when something looks wrong, and the game marks the spot for Jared."]},{"id":"app-icon","date":"2026-11-05","lines":["A new picture for the game: the Iron Knight by the camp fire at nightfall."]},{"id":"desktop-app","date":"2026-11-05","lines":["Iron Wasteland 2 is now an app on the Mac, with Single Player, Host for the Family, and a list of family games to join. No typing an address.","Pick Live or Dev on the start screen. New versions download by themselves.","The game can be installed like an app and plays with no internet.","The Gunslinger can pistol-whip up close.","Raider camp fires now cook food."]},{"id":"world-grows","date":"2026-11-04","lines":["Play together: two to five computers on the home network share one world, and downed friends can be revived.","Chop trees, gather scrap and fibre, and craft food, medicine, ammo and tools.","Build walls, gates and spike traps. Raiders and creatures can break walls down.","Day turns to night, with weather in every land, and nights are harder. Sleep in a bed to skip ahead.","A serpent lives in the lake, and a long fall now hurts."]},{"id":"first-world","date":"2026-11-03","lines":["A new 3D world with five characters and seven lands, from the waste to the frozen north.","You start in a safe valley ringed by mountains, with a camp and a fire that heals.","Ruined towns, raider camps and houses you can walk into, and a tower with a ladder to climb.","Wolves, bears, rats and worse, and you can climb onto rocks, crates and roofs."]}],"noteIds":["screens-style-nov15","quality-pass-nov15","worlds-fix-nov15","start-menu-nov15","torches-stumps-nov14","running-water-nov14","houses-nov14","spider-poison-nov14","places-nov14","switch-and-giveup-nov14","spiders-nov14","repair-nov14","game-modes-nov14","harder-and-fixes-nov14","house-porches","fog-of-war","hunters-and-rocks","creatures-pass","background-music","fireflies","health-number","random-worlds","play-logs","app-icon","desktop-app","world-grows","first-world"],"files":{"index.html":{"size":37875,"sha256":"938304501a0d8ff0eb30ef5bbdac8aea2f3bb44a7ca6e24bcd1ac472bed8269e"},"manifest.webmanifest":{"size":572,"sha256":"4fd9ecc79e7b84fe184382e71d2647002ac121ef04d8561443e11910b8eb4372"},"sw.js":{"size":4918,"sha256":"1cd782efdeafd7e3d9f448ea511ef96acbe1a59a6a3e4daaa80a6e5f63e19eb2"},"src/arrows.js":{"size":3450,"sha256":"e1988eb1c6e72782ad08cfbdca0260e0732e34a489fe3b41c992edcc2676c56e"},"src/audio.js":{"size":23081,"sha256":"729840c9657cb9f1256779f3fffe2e22fb71715f58ff1f42f53fe3ee3c3216bf"},"src/bear.js":{"size":15070,"sha256":"25d2940605a9475fbd07cba0b85d7a54731e0850231906b13a743ab29f431174"},"src/bog.js":{"size":4615,"sha256":"d85f8c7a576cf8e7df485bf0136871c29bbda144cd9816ddde18b52dd448a39c"},"src/build.js":{"size":34045,"sha256":"053d8a621c8ccbb16253c2c5cf436cbfa908f3662093c3f85ed5aab813b2408e"},"src/buildings.js":{"size":218291,"sha256":"92595291909ee37073ba1c380745b77825ad050b7aed9b2361c66c87d7e5555c"},"src/buildmodels.js":{"size":11199,"sha256":"d183109e3643218ad